--[============[
asi_single.lua -- the COMPLETE project in ONE Lua 5.4 file (every module, every test, the immutable handoff, the CLI).

HOW TO USE (Replit or any Lua 5.4):
  1. Create a Repl (Lua), open  main.lua,  select all, paste this whole file, save.
  2. Click Run:   with no arguments it runs a short quick-start (help, risk lemmas, parity, shared reasoning, five test suites).
  3. In the Shell, run any command (replace main.lua by your file name):
        lua main.lua selftest                  all registered suites, including the shared reasoning regressions
        lua main.lua selftest world vm risk    selected suites:  math rng validate world vm gl risk proof parity twin mutation harness
        lua main.lua validate --fast           handoff validation + the independent exact finite-law validator
        lua main.lua episode --controller asi --world sample:1001      one full network episode with the complete controller
        lua main.lua episode --controller diag_all --world extreme:hot:1001
        lua main.lua parity --mode full --seed 2001                    one parity-exception episode
        lua main.lua reason --family symbolic --seed 1                 the metered shared reasoner
        lua main.lua reason-compare --held --ablations --budgets       frozen finite-task evaluation to stdout
        lua main.lua reason-report                                    architecture audit and measured evidence
        lua main.lua compare --only parity --limit 8 --out out.lua     part of the pre-registered evaluation (writes a Lua-table report)
        lua main.lua report out.lua            read a report;   lua main.lua replay out.lua --row 1   re-run a row, check its trace hash
        lua main.lua prompt                    print the implementation prompt embedded in the handoff
        lua main.lua help
  4. To make the Run button do something else, edit  DEFAULT_ARGS  in the last section of this file, e.g.
        local DEFAULT_ARGS = {"selftest"}
  Exit status: 0 = everything demanded held, 1 = violated invariant / failed check, 2 = rejected input.

REQUIREMENTS: Lua 5.4 (64-bit integers). Nothing else: no packages, no network, no other language, no files (the handoff is
embedded). If the console says "Lua 5.4 is required", switch the Repl to a Lua 5.4 interpreter and run again.
The large pre-registered evaluation (972 jobs) takes hours on one core; the finished report of that run is a separate data file
(reports/evidence.lua) that is not part of this program.

CONTENTS: the preserved and upgraded sources below are wrapped as package.preload entries; bundle_info hashes the current bodies:
