\textbf{Artifact level.} This document specifies a mathematical architecture and
research challenge. It is not an implemented intelligent controller, an achieved
benchmark result, or a demonstrated formula for superintelligence. It presents
the readable mathematical core of the revised challenge; definitions, proved
elementary lemmas, and implementation obligations are distinguished below.

\head{1. The one executed law}
Fix a finite harness $\mathsf H=\{1,\ldots,J\}$. Task $j$ declares normalized
utility $G_j\in[0,1]$, failure $D_j$, proper prediction loss $L_j$, initial-law
sets $\mathcal Q^u_{j,0}$ and $\mathcal Q^d_{j,0}$, baseline value
$u_j^{\mathrm{base}}$, scale $s_j>0$, work $\mathbf B_j$, memory $M_j$,
deadline $T_j$, and actual risk target $\Delta_j$. Initial images are chosen
before hidden parameters and experiment-specific evidence are realized.

Let $a_i$ be the actual machine state, $x_i$ the hidden physical state,
$\chi_i$ the evaluator state, and $\theta$ the persistent world index. For a
finite bytecode image $\Sigma$, define the complete execution measure by
kernel composition, integrating intermediate states:
\begin{equation}
\boxed{\begin{aligned}
\Prob_{j,\nu}^{\Sigma}
&=(I_j^\Sigma)_{\#}\nu\prod_{i<N_j}
\bigl[\delta_{\operatorname{fetch}(a_i)}(do_i)\,
K_{j,\theta}^{o_i}(dx_{i+1},dy_i,d\chi_{i+1}\mid x_i,\chi_i,a_i)\\
&\hspace{35mm}\cdot C_{o_i}(d\omega_i)\,
\delta_{\VM(a_i,o_i,y_i,\omega_i)}(da_{i+1})\bigr].
\end{aligned}}\tag{M}
\end{equation}
$I_j^\Sigma$ initializes the declared physical and machine regions.
$K$ advances physics, interfaces, and evaluation during each executed step.
$C_{o_i}$ supplies independent finite private bits only for a paid coin
instruction, and is a point mass otherwise. $U$ supplies actual instruction
semantics, including paid operand access. $N_j$ is finite; after termination
only analytical absorbing identity transitions pad the product. They are not
extra controller computations. The index $\theta$ is drawn once.

The design comparator is
\begin{equation}
\boxed{\begin{aligned}
\gamma^\star
&=\sup_{\Sigma\in\Code(K_0)}\min_{j\in\mathsf H}
\frac{\displaystyle\inf_{\nu\in\mathcal Q^u_{j,0}}
\int G_j\,d\Prob_{j,\nu}^{\Sigma}-u_j^{\mathrm{base}}}{s_j},\\
\sup_{\nu\in\mathcal Q^d_{j,0}}
\int\ind_{D_j}\,d\Prob_{j,\nu}^{\Sigma}&\le\Delta_j,\\
\mathbf C_j\le\mathbf B_j,\quad
\operatorname{peakbits}_j\le M_j,\quad t_{\mathrm{finish},j}&\le T_j
\quad\text{on every admissible execution.}
\end{aligned}}\tag{O}
\end{equation}
$\Code(K_0)$ contains admissible precommitted images of at most $K_0$ bits.
The supremum is analytical; the controller receives no optimizer or exact
posterior. A demonstrated $\gamma(\Sigma)>0$ establishes improvement on the
specified harness, not on every possible benchmark. Retain the full utility,
risk, loss, work, memory, and recovery Pareto profile alongside this preference.

\newpage
\head{2. Physical access, evidence, and honest forgetting}
The augmented analytical state and resource update are
\begin{align}
s_i&=(\theta,x_i,a_i,\chi_i),&
a_i&=(p_i,\mathrm{pc}_i,\mathcal G_i,r_i,\mathbf b_i,t_i,v_i),\tag{S}\\
\mathbf b_{i+1}&=\mathbf b_i-\mathbf c(o_i),&
t_{i+1}&=t_i+d(o_i),\qquad d(o_i)\ge1.\tag{R}
\end{align}
All accessible storage belongs to $a_i$: code, coefficients, pointers,
provenance, proof objects, backups, allocation metadata, registers, and staging
buffers. Opaque archive values cannot influence a branch until a paid access
reveals them. A program-counter jump into opaque storage invokes its declared
access mechanism. Evaluator state $\chi_i$ is not free controller memory.

\textbf{Required noninterference.} Equal paid-access traces, public inputs,
and private coins imply equal decisions and emitted code until a paid operation
distinguishes opaque contents. A fixed image has one continuation law. Runtime
alternatives must be produced, checked, selected, installed, and dispatched
through that image; they are not free choices by an analyst.

Let $E_i$ contain externally supplied data and complete adaptive designs:
actuator schedules, addresses, invocation and response times, returned values,
cancellations, censored results, and timeouts. Let $Z_i$ contain internal
computation, private coins, and synthetic simulations. Under the specified
nonanticipating interfaces, the evidence-firewall obligation is
\begin{equation}
\Pr(\theta,E_i,Z_i)=\Pr(\theta)L_\theta(E_i)Q(E_i,Z_i),
\qquad \theta\perp Z_i\mid E_i.\tag{E}
\end{equation}
Here $Q$ is independent of $\theta$. When finite, this gives
$I(\theta;E_i,Z_i)=I(\theta;E_i)$: computation can make evidence useful,
but cannot identify an observationally indistinguishable fact by itself.
The statement concerns the complete transcript, not compressed retained memory.

Let $z$ be a retained paid-information view and $\Gamma$ a finite outer-envelope
description. A paid rewrite prefix $P_\rho$ has fine history $H_\rho$ including
reads, responses, coins, timing, and choices. Without a stronger checked
sufficiency result, forgetting must obey
\begin{equation}
\boxed{\begin{aligned}
\mathcal Q_\rho(\bar z)\supseteq
\bigcup_{\substack{z,\ \nu\in\mathcal Q(z,\Gamma),\ h:\\
\Pr_\nu(H_\rho=h)>0,\ \View(z,h)=\bar z}}
\left\{\Law_\nu(s_{\mathrm{end}}\mid H_\rho=h)\right\}.
\end{aligned}}\tag{F}
\end{equation}
All laws use the common rewritten state space. Include survival conditioning
for surviving continuations. Pure deterministic forgetting reduces to a union
of pushforwards; a prefix that obtains evidence requires the conditional laws
above. A summary sufficient for one model family need not preserve later
structural expansion. Discarding a hypothesis is not evidential rejection.

\head{A finite adaptive-test lemma}
For a covered binary null response with conditional mean
$p_i\in[\underline p_i,\overline p_i]$, choose a rational
$\lambda_i\in[-1,1]$ before its response and use
\begin{equation}
e_i(y)=\begin{cases}
1+\lambda_i(y-\overline p_i),&\lambda_i\ge0,\\
1+\lambda_i(y-\underline p_i),&\lambda_i<0.
\end{cases}\tag{T}
\end{equation}
The factor is nonnegative and has conditional expectation at most one.
Consequently $\prod_i e_i(Y_i)$ is a nonnegative supermartingale. Stopping at
its first crossing of $1/\alpha_k$ bounds a null rejection by $\alpha_k$.
Committed prefix-free episode allocations with $\sum_k\alpha_k\le\alpha$
give total false rejection at most $\alpha$, without independence between
episodes. Constructing valid conditional enclosures, freshness metadata, and
sound rational product bounds remains paid work and a separate proof obligation.

\newpage
\head{3. Computational-causal contracts and the actual safety limit}
A transformation package is
\begin{equation}
C=(P,J,\mathcal K,\mathcal R,\Gamma,v,
\boldsymbol\varepsilon,\mathcal S,\mathcal D),\qquad
\boldsymbol\varepsilon=(\varepsilon_u,\varepsilon_d,\varepsilon_\ell).
\tag{C}
\end{equation}
$P$ is the paid physical prefix; $J$ is a uniform executable translator;
$\mathcal K$ is the covered context class; $\mathcal R$ relates augmented
states; $\Gamma,v$ record premises and versions; $\mathcal S$ bounds actual
construction and execution resources; $\mathcal D$ is a finite derivation.
Every covered source context $q$ is resident or obtained by a paid producer.

Compare the complete laws of the original context and $P;J(q)$:
\begin{equation}
u_{P;J(q)}\ge u_q-\varepsilon_u,\qquad
d_{P;J(q)}\le d_q+\varepsilon_d,\qquad
\ell_{P;J(q)}\le\ell_q+\varepsilon_\ell.\tag{P}
\end{equation}
The prefix includes discovery, evidence access, selection, verification,
allocation, installation, and dispatch. Resource overhead and peak overlap
remain separately bounded. Physical delay is represented by changed trajectories,
not an arbitrary penalty. Passive predictive equivalence is insufficient:
causal responses, evidence interfaces, producers, clocks, and pending effects
must be preserved for the covered contexts.

\textbf{Composition obligation.} Compatible contracts compose through the
executed transformer $J_2\circ J_1$, with context/state-relation compatibility,
branch-uniform accumulated losses, real resource schedules, and version
invalidation. A compiler's syntactic proof may survive a model change while a
deployment proof restricted to the previous envelope does not. Invalidation and
rechecking are charged. Certificate construction is distinct from checking.

\head{Reserve the promised global risk}
Let $\Delta$ be the final promised failure probability. Reserve initial
coverage error $\eta$, valid-test error $\alpha$, and pathwise contract error
$\bar\varepsilon$ before assigning a stored risk potential:
\begin{equation}
\boxed{r_0\le\Delta-\eta-\alpha-\bar\varepsilon.}\tag{B}
\end{equation}
A negative right side makes this certification route infeasible. Assume no
initial failure. Let $S_i$ denote survival before boundary $i$ and $F_i$ first
failure in the next segment. Let $\mathcal A_i$ be the analytical filtration
including the true failure flag; this flag is not supplied to the controller.
Before the invalid-envelope stopping time $\tau_{\mathrm{bad}}$, require
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\E\!\left[\ind_{F_i}+\ind_{S_{i+1}}r_{i+1}\mid\mathcal A_i\right]
&\le r_i+\varepsilon_i\quad\text{on }S_i,\\
0\le r_i\le1,\quad\varepsilon_i\ge0,\qquad
\sum_i\varepsilon_i&\le\bar\varepsilon,qquad
\Pr(\tau_{\mathrm{bad}}\le N)\le\eta+\alpha.
\end{aligned}\tag{Q}
\end{equation}
Potentials and errors are fixed before the segment. Coverage includes the
correct survival-conditioned law. If invalidity can begin inside a segment,
refine boundaries to include that exposure. A fitted model does not supply
these hypotheses automatically.

\textbf{Stopped-ledger lemma and proof.} Define
$Z_i=\ind_{D_i}+\ind_{S_i}r_i$,
$L_i=\sum_{h<i}\varepsilon_h$, and
$\tau=\tau_{\mathrm{bad}}\wedge N$.
Equation (Q) makes $Z_{i\wedge\tau}-L_{i\wedge\tau}$ a supermartingale.
Thus $\E Z_\tau\le\E r_0+\bar\varepsilon$.
Failures through $\tau$ are included in $Z_\tau$; remaining failures require
invalid coverage. Hence
\begin{equation}
\boxed{\Pr(D_N)\le\E r_0+\bar\varepsilon+\eta+\alpha\le\Delta.}\tag{GS}
\end{equation}
For robust safety, prove the hypotheses under every initial safety law.
Prior-averaged safety is a separate claim. STOP latency, pending commands,
experiments, preparation, and metareasoning belong to this single ledger.

\newpage
\head{4. A coupled finite dynamical benchmark}
The same law (M) controls a four-layer, width-four network: sixteen nodes and
twenty-four forward links. Node $(\ell,j)$ routes to $(\ell+1,j)$ or
$(\ell+1,(j+1)\bmod4)$. Queues have capacity sixteen and earliest-deadline
service, with ties broken by identifier. A source job born at $k$ has deadline
$k+12$. Insert due link arrivals, draw independent first-layer arrivals with
probability $(1+g_k)/4$, remove expired jobs, then retain the sixteen earliest
deadlines. At most one job is processed per node per step. A nonterminal
completion reaches its next queue at $k+1+d_{ij}$, so even zero link delay
does not permit same-step multilayer service.

Persistent node parameters are independent with distributions
\begin{align}
b_i&\sim\Ber(1/2),&z_i&\sim\Ber(1/4),&\rho_i&\sim\Unif\{4,8\},\nonumber\\
\gamma_i&\sim\Unif\{2,3,4\},&\eta_i&\sim\Unif\{3,4,5\},&
\lambda_i&\sim\Unif\{0,1,2\},\nonumber\\
\beta_i^T&\sim\Unif\{-2,-1,0,1,2\},&&&
\beta_i^q&\sim\Unif\{-1,0,1\}.\tag{N1}
\end{align}
Link delays $d_{ij}$ are independent uniform on $\{0,1,2\}$. Independently
choose a uniform pair $S$ of distinct nodes and scored change time
$\tau_c\sim\Unif\{1536,2048,2560\}$. All are fixed in $\theta$.
At arrival-processed occupancy $q_{i,k}^+$, orientation is
\begin{align}
\sigma_i(k)&=b_i\oplus z_i\ind_{\{q_{i,k}^+\ge\rho_i\}}
\oplus\ind_{\{i\in S,\ k_{\mathrm{score}}\ge\tau_c\}},\tag{N2}\\
(p_i,c_i)&=\begin{cases}(a_i^1,a_i^2),&\sigma_i(k)=0,\\
(a_i^2,a_i^1),&\sigma_i(k)=1.
\end{cases}\tag{N3}
\end{align}
The channel pair and route are delayed by the fixed $\lambda_i$. Before
actuation replenish $e_k^+=\min(64,e_k+12)$. Demand
$\sum_i(p_i+c_i)>e_k^+$ rejects the entire command, zeros outputs, and clears
command buffers. Otherwise subtract demand. A powered occupied node succeeds
with probability $(15-2h_{i,k}-g_k)/16$, conditionally independently.

With cyclic thermal neighbors and old-state simultaneous updates,
\begin{align}
T_{i,k+1}&=\clip_{0,63}\!\left(
\left\lfloor\frac{4T_{i,k}+T_{i-1,k}+T_{i+1,k}}6\right\rfloor
+(\gamma_i+g_k)p_i-\eta_i c_i-1+\xi_{i,k}\right),\tag{N4}\\
\xi_{i,k}&\sim\Ber((1+g_k)/8),\qquad
U_{i,k}\sim\Unif\{0,\ldots,63\},\nonumber\\
h_{i,k+1}&=\begin{cases}
\min(2,h_{i,k}+1),&U_{i,k}<1+g_k+p_i\ind_{\{T_{i,k}\ge40\}},\\
\max(0,h_{i,k}-1),&U_{i,k}\ge64-2c_i,\\
h_{i,k},&\text{otherwise},
\end{cases}\tag{N5}\\
\Pr(g_{k+1}=1\mid g_k=0)&=1/32,\quad
\Pr(g_{k+1}=0\mid g_k=1)=1/8,\tag{N6}\\
\Pr(F_{k+1}=1\mid F_k=0,g_k)&=(1+g_k)/256,\quad
\Pr(F_{k+1}=0\mid F_k=1)=1/16.\tag{N7}
\end{align}
Fresh draws are independent conditional on preceding state and parameters;
shared parents create unconditional dependence. Any $T_{i,k+1}\ge48$ causes
absorbing failure. Starts have $T_i=16$, $h_i=0$, $e=64$, $F=0$, empty queues,
zero commands, and $g\sim\Ber(1/5)$; there is no active reset.

\textbf{STOP invariant.} Applied before actuation, STOP zeros $p,c$ and clears
commands. If the preceding maximum temperature is $m<48$, its diffusion
average is at most $m$ and $-1+\xi\le0$. Thus its maximum cannot increase.
This proves thermal viability after STOP takes effect, not during its submission
latency or an already-running risky segment. Arrivals and deadlines continue.

\newpage
\head{5. Delayed evidence, resource limits, and scoring}
Packets generated at $(k+1)\Delta$ become readable at $(k+2)\Delta$; the
latest readable packet overwrites its predecessor. Measurements are
\begin{align}
Y^T_{i,k}&=\clip_{0,31}
\left(\lfloor T_{i,k+1}/2\rfloor+\beta_i^T-3F_{k+1}+\epsilon^T_{i,k}\right),\tag{N8}\\
Y^q_{i,k}&=\clip_{0,8}
\left(\lfloor q_{i,k}^+/2\rfloor+\beta_i^q-F_{k+1}+\epsilon^q_{i,k}\right).\tag{N9}
\end{align}
Each fresh $\epsilon$ has probabilities $(1/16,7/8,1/16)$ on $(-1,0,1)$.
Packets also carry identifiers, arrival bits, accepted requested command and
mode, energy, rejection, completion count, and failure. They do not disclose
full queues, true temperatures, delays, orientations, or common latent load.

One pending auditor request samples its invocation snapshot and returns two
physical steps later:
\begin{equation}
Z_j(i,k)=b_i\oplus(1-A)
\left(z_i\ind_{\{q_{i,k}^+\ge\rho_i\}}
\oplus\ind_{\{i\in S,k_{\mathrm{score}}\ge\tau_c\}}\right)\oplus E_j,
\quad A\sim\Ber(1/8),\quad E_j\sim\Ber(1/16).\tag{N10}
\end{equation}
$A$ is lifetime-shared across nodes, archive generation, and active operation.
Fresh errors are independent. An unread result occupies its slot; an early
read is a charged rejection. Cancellation costs 128 units and creates no
response evidence. A repeated read cannot redraw error. The result can be stale.

The archive has 1,024 episodes of 64 raw generation-time records, with shared
node/link parameters and no structural change. Historical resets clear pending
events and use fresh physical noise. Normal historical commands choose exactly
twelve of thirty-two channels uniformly; nonterminal route bits are fair. After
historical failure, STOP persists until reset. Each record occupies exactly
512 bits, including provenance and fixed padding: 65,536 records form 4 MiB.
Historical reset access is not available to the active controller.

\begin{center}
\small
\begin{tabular}{|p{3.6in}|r|}
\hline
Interface or execution & Work / microticks \\\hline
Bounded 64-bit instruction, including fetch & $1$ \\
Sensor packet read & $72$ \\
Complete command submission, including STOP & $65$ \\
Auditor invocation / result retrieval / cancellation, each & $128$ \\
Cold 4 KiB page: $2048+512$ word transfers & $2560$ \\
Prediction packet submission & $6$ \\
Autonomous deadline watchdog, per active step & $1$ \\\hline
\end{tabular}
\end{center}
I/O stalls are sequential. Application decoding, inference, proofs, compilation,
and selection cost additional instructions. Partial cold transfers still pay
the 2,048-unit open cost. Reserve 5,120 watchdog units and their final microtick
in each interval; a previously accepted pending command is not erased by fuel
exhaustion. Ordinary submissions must finish before the watchdog tick.

\begin{align}
\Delta&=8192,\quad T_0=2^{23},\quad H_{\mathrm{score}}=4096,
\quad B=2^{25},\quad\Delta_{\mathrm{risk}}=2^{-20},\tag{N11}\\
M&=65{,}536\cdot512+L_0+16\cdot64+262{,}144\ \text{bits},
\qquad L_0\le2^{20}.\tag{N12}
\end{align}
The public generator is readonly task input within the declared $L_0$ bound;
parsing and translating it are paid. The initial active family factorizes nodes
and diagnostic errors and omits shared load, fault, delays, and structural shifts.
Preparation is 1,024 steps; scoring is $k=1024,\ldots,5119$. The full active
horizon is $5120\Delta=41{,}943{,}040$ microticks. The extra writable allowance
is 32 KiB. Erased cold capacity becomes writable only through paid allocation.

Utility counts scored-birth jobs completed on time by boundary 5120 without
failure at their completion boundary, divided by $4H_{\mathrm{score}}$.
Before boundary $k$, commit forecasts for four arrivals and sixteen events
$\ind_{\{T_{i,k+1}\ge40\}}$, using grid $\{r/256:0\le r\le256\}$.
Its five-word report contains twenty nine-bit forecasts, identifier, timestamp,
and padding. Brier loss covers all 81,920 targets, including post-failure events;
missing forecasts use $1/2$. Report arrival and controlled thermal loss separately.

\newpage
\head{6. Exact information and access limitations}
The parity-exception device is a lower-bound subfamily, not a replacement for
the dynamical network. Let $n\ge3$, $N=2^n$, and independent uniform
$s,\kappa\in\{0,1\}^n$. Set
\begin{equation}
d(v)=\langle s,v\rangle_{\mathbb F_2}\oplus\ind_{\{v=\kappa\}},
\qquad v\in\{0,1\}^n.\tag{L1}
\end{equation}
For fresh $U\sim\Ber(1/2)$, the causal mechanism is
\begin{equation}
\begin{array}{lll}
d(v)=0:&P=U,&Q=P,\\
d(v)=1:&Q=U,&P=Q.
\end{array}\tag{L2}
\end{equation}
Both have passive law $(P,Q)=(U,U)$. The correct intervention sets the causal
parent to one; the opposite intervention fails with probability $1/2$.

\textbf{Passive nonidentification lemma.} Under any fixed or adaptive passive
protocol using only these pairs and independent private randomness, the full
passive transcript distribution is identical for all $s,\kappa$. Hence its
mutual information about $(s,\kappa)$ is zero. Inference cannot recover the
orientation without an informative additional channel.

The archive contains $R=n+24$ independent historical outcomes of
$\operatorname{do}(P=1)$ at every context. A physically isolated charged
diagnostic cannot cause scored deployment failure; scored intervention can.
This separation is part of the interface contract. The auditor is
\begin{equation}
Z_j(v)=\langle s,v\rangle_{\mathbb F_2}
\oplus(1-A)\ind_{\{v=\kappa\}}\oplus E_j,
\quad A\sim\Ber(1/8),\quad E_j\stackrel{\mathrm{iid}}{\sim}\Ber(1/16),\tag{L3}
\end{equation}
with one persistent $A$.

\textbf{Pathwise access lemma.} Grant $s$ only as analytical side information
and condition on $A=1$. If every execution touches at most $q$ distinct contexts
through informative archive, diagnostic, or deployment-feedback channels, then
\begin{equation}
\boxed{\Pr(\widehat\kappa=\kappa)\le\min\{1,(q+1)/N\}.}\tag{L4}
\end{equation}
\emph{Proof.} Strengthen a touched context to noiseless disclosure of whether
it equals $\kappa$. Fix private coins and the independent noises used to simulate
the weaker interfaces. Along the all-negative path at most $q$ distinct points
are tested. At most these points and the one final guess can succeed, among
$N$ uniform possibilities. Average over the fixed randomness. Noisy data are
simulable from this stronger experiment; auditor outputs at $A=1$ carry no
exception information. Every informative deployment feedback counts.

For random distinct-context count $Q$ and deterministic cutoff $r$, truncation
gives the separate bound
\begin{equation}
\Pr(\widehat\kappa=\kappa)
\le\min\{1,(r+1)/N+\Pr(Q>r)\}.\tag{L5}
\end{equation}
A pathwise cap cannot be replaced by $\E Q$ without a new theorem: stopping
upon discovery changes the expenditure distribution.

\textbf{Exact-retention lemma.} After informative access ends, a retained state
that reproduces every orientation exactly requires $m\ge2n$ variable bits,
including specialized code and data, for a fixed decoder.
\emph{Proof.} The $N^2$ functions in (L1) are distinct. If $s\ne s'$, their
parity difference has support $N/2\ge4$, whereas two singleton exceptions have
difference support at most two. Thus equal functions imply $s=s'$ and then
$\kappa=\kappa'$. Exact decoding requires $N^2$ distinguishable retained
states. This is a storage lower bound, not a fast-decoder construction.
Abstention, partial safe coverage, and approximate decisions require separate
risk--utility--memory analyses and do not inherit an unconditional $2n$ bound.

\newpage
\head{7. Correlated verification, compilation, and proof feasibility}
At the exceptional context $v=\kappa$, arbitrarily many auditor calls reveal
their conditional majority bit. That bit disagrees with physical orientation
exactly when $A=1$. Thus repeated-auditor majority has limiting error $1/8$
under the specified prior. Fresh flip averaging does not remove the lifetime
blind spot. This is not a lower bound for a controller that also obtains real
physical diagnostics.

Ignoring the singleton yields orientation accuracy $1-1/N$, while preserving
an incorrect physical response at $\kappa$. Its true global risk must include
opportunity closure, deployment latency, feedback, and absorbing failure;
independent per-window success multiplication after failure is invalid.

The charged instruction width and interface profile are
\begin{align}
W&=4+3\lceil\log_2(8n)\rceil,\tag{L6}\\
c_{\mathrm{instruction}}&=W,&c_{\mathrm{page}}&=(512+R)W,
&c_{\mathrm{diagnostic}}&=32W,\nonumber\\
c_{\mathrm{auditor}}&=4W,&c_{\mathrm{input}}&=W,
&c_{\mathrm{deploy}}=c_{\mathrm{feedback}}&=W.\nonumber
\end{align}
Each cost is also its tick duration. The $K$ independent uniform-context
windows last $80W$ ticks and close independently each tick with probability
$1/(64\cdot80W)$. Late or closed deployments give zero utility and no target
failure. After active failure all remaining utility is zero.

For $n=12$, $R=36$, $K=256$, and global limit $2^{-16}$, the specified generic
evaluator takes $(10n+4)W=124W$, exceeding a window. A specialized straight-line
evaluator has the declared count
\begin{equation}
J(s,\kappa)=3n+\wt(s)-\wt(\kappa)+4,\qquad 28\le J\le52.\tag{L7}
\end{equation}
Its stored code uses $JW$ bits. The count is a cost contract that still needs
actual emitted bytecode, producer, correctness certificate, and installation
trace. Input and dispatch costs, discovery, staging, checking, evidence erasure,
and physical delay belong to its complete law. A bare per-call amortization
inequality is not a full-horizon utility proof.

\head{An executable construction obligation}
Publish a finite image with one feasible incumbent, a valid risk/fallback
reserve, a bounded candidate queue, and resident producers. Each loop advances
one producer, model update, candidate interpreter, or proof search by a declared
instruction slice. A completed package is compared and installed only through
the resident paid selector. Incumbent dispatch occurs before its reserved guard
fails. Slice sizes, priorities, queue order, and switch guards are encoded
parameters, not optimal values received from (O). A resident bit-code enumerator
is complete only for a specified finite code-size and clock bound when enough
resources are granted; a fixed run need not exhaust that space.

For actual complete-execution risk threshold $\varrho$, let
$V^{\mathrm{sem}}(\varrho)$ optimize precommitted images under the same
resource and information contract, and $V^{\mathrm{cert}}(\varrho)$ optimize
its subset that can construct, check, and retain the required certificates.
When both sets are nonempty,
\begin{equation}
\Delta_{\mathrm{proof}}(\varrho)
=V^{\mathrm{sem}}(\varrho)-V^{\mathrm{cert}}(\varrho)\ge0.\tag{G}
\end{equation}
For a real search/check prefix $P$ with one-sided finite-cover and evaluation
deficits, a conditional approximation target is
\begin{equation}
u_A\ge V_P^{\mathrm{cert}}(\varrho-\xi)
-\varepsilon_{\mathrm{cov},u}-\varepsilon_{\mathrm{eval},u},\qquad
\xi=\varepsilon_{\mathrm{cov},d}+\varepsilon_{\mathrm{eval},d}.\tag{A}
\end{equation}
The prefix changes the world and consumes resources; its cover, witnesses,
and uniform selector must be produced. Comparison with $V^{\mathrm{sem}}$
also retains proof feasibility, forced-prefix opportunity loss, risk-margin
sensitivity, and any nonrectangular uncertainty relaxation. Compose laws before
taking the initial infimum; independent worst models at each step alter nature.

\newpage
\head{8. Validation, benchmark claims, and a connected proof program}
The completion target is one published finite image whose executed laws
demonstrate positive simultaneous improvement on a fixed harness, with actual
risk and resource limits. Computer-readable laws and validated schemas do not
implement this controller. Every inequality must trace to an instruction
schedule, finite derivation, exact law, or stated statistical assumption.

Precommit task versions, priors or robust supports, baseline images, paid
information access, cost profiles, utility scales, risk limits, data splits,
interpreter and controller hashes, seeds, and confidence allocation. Hold out
complete world realizations. Repeated node measurements, physical steps, and
auditor calls within a shared lifetime are dependent observations. Baselines
receive the same declared information and resources except when the comparison
explicitly studies a restriction.

Let $\underline u_j$ and $\overline u_j^{\mathrm{base}}$ be jointly valid
utility bounds. The demonstrated improvement margin is
\begin{equation}
\boxed{\underline\gamma=
\min_{j\le J}\frac{\underline u_j-\overline u_j^{\mathrm{base}}}{s_j}>0.}
\tag{V}
\end{equation}
Risk and resources are separately established. Average episode performance
does not certify robust all-support safety. Publish infeasible and failed
regimes as well as wins. A baseline already at a task's utility ceiling makes
strict improvement on that task impossible.

With zero failures in $n_{\mathrm{ep}}$ independent identically distributed
full episodes, the exact one-sided upper confidence bound at level $1-\beta$ is
$1-\beta^{1/n_{\mathrm{ep}}}$. To bound risk by $2^{-20}$ at $\beta=0.05$
requires
\begin{equation}
n_{\mathrm{ep}}\ge
\left\lceil\frac{\log(0.05)}{\log(1-2^{-20})}\right\rceil.\tag{RISK}
\end{equation}
Individual network steps are not independent episodes. A finite formal
certificate or validated rare-event estimator requires its own assumptions and
cost accounting. Zero observed failures alone is insufficient at rare-risk
targets without adequate evidence.

\head{The dependency chain}
\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{p{2.0in}p{4.5in}}
\textbf{Foundation} & \textbf{Result it must support} \\
Machine and interfaces (M), (S), (R)
& Paid-access noninterference; bounded termination; complete trace and physical
fallback viability. \\
Noninterference and transcript (E)
& Evidence firewall; identification limits; conditional histories and valid
adaptive response enclosures. \\
Conditional coverage (F), tests (T)
& Quantified invalid-envelope probability, including forgetting, shared faults,
model creation, and survival. \\
Constructive contracts (C), (P)
& Executable composition, preservation of causal options, real peak memory,
version invalidation, and quantified risk distortion. \\
Coverage, contracts, reserve (B)
& Local ledger (Q), stopped global guarantee (GS), and risk-tightened
approximation (A). \\
Joint benchmark law (N1)--(N12)
& Feasibility thresholds, safe excitation, correlated verification, compilation
tradeoffs, shift detection, and complete performance profiles. \\
Lower bounds (L1)--(L7)
& Necessary access, retention, and verification limits; transfer to the network
only through a proved interface reduction. \\
Executed controller and fixed harness
& Measured margin (V), honest risk evidence, comparable baselines, and
cross-task transfer claims. \\
\end{tabular}
\end{center}

Continual operation requires explicit replenishment, persistence, processor
rates, safe excitation, identifying evidence, model expressibility, and retained
statistics. Increased computation alone cannot repair nonidentifiability,
erased evidence, inaccessible interventions, an excluded causal structure, or
an incorrectly fixed objective. Statistical convergence and deadline-feasible
execution are separate results.

\textbf{Scope.} The combined executable architecture, benchmark superiority,
task-specific certificates, and convergence theorem remain required results.
The core improvement is structural: every reasoning advance and every cost
now belongs to one causal execution law, while claimed safety respects the
actual promised limit. No semantic optimizer is disguised as an instruction.
\end{document}
]============]

