asi/guest/pctrl.lua -- guest controllers (VM-1 programs) for the parity-exception subfamily.

Every instruction below is charged W work and W ticks by the machine; every interface call is paid in full.
The controller sees only what its paid instructions return (no hidden parameter, orientation label or compiled answer).

MODES (cfg.mode)
  "full"        learn s from n archive pages (d(e_i) = s_i unless kappa = e_i), verify the parity model against
                CHK further archive pages and the hypothesis set {no exception, kappa = a mismatching check,
                s flipped at i with kappa = e_i}; if no exception is visible, SCAN every context with the
                auditor (majority of up to 3 calls disagreeing with <s,v>), confirm every candidate with the
                archive page (d(v) != <s,v> proves v = kappa, error 2^-R), then COMPILE the specialised
                evaluator (paid bytecode emission), CHECK it (sandbox grammar + structural conformance to
